From 7caff3125a452ce9d6739d6fcfef1b9af9b790aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 18:42:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(motion): keep the plain level law on the rotary
 air-split ladder

The shallow-floor discovery of #2088 also ran in pocket3d_air_split,
which only the rotary wrap calls. In the wrap a flat face is a turned
skin, so the discovery added a level at the foot of the window v 0..8,
and rotary_offset::the_height_window_names_the_stations_and_refuses_an_empty_one
got a toolpath where the law says air. The air-split ladder now uses
cut_levels_under again. The pin
blind_floor::the_rotary_air_split_ladder_keeps_the_plain_level_law shows
that pocket3d cuts the shallow floor and the air-split ladder refuses it.

Refs #2088

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
